!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-ports.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A sparse numeric member set on each exact tier ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.6). `members` is the spelling for a
  value set that is neither a contiguous range nor an arithmetic progression, and so is expressible by
  none of the other facets the numeric families carry: an HTTP status subset, a protobuf enum's explicit
  numbers, the three ports below. §7.4 rules the enum out for them -- an enum member is an identifier --
  which is what leaves the facet to do the work.

  The two families are here together because their identity rules read differently and must not: an
  integer member set compares whole numbers, where a decimal one compares numbers that carry a scale, and
  [TSON-DATA] §4.3 makes `2.50` and `2.5` one value in both.
  """
{
  port  => !integer ^ { members: [80 443 8080] }
  price => !number ^ { members: [1 2.50] }

  listing => {
    p: port
    q: price
  }
}
